{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Dan will judge his people</b> — as in \"for YHWH will judge His people\" (Deuteronomy 32:36), \"for YHWH will judge the judgment of His people,\" in the language of \"Judge me, O YHWH, and plead my cause against a nation that is not devout\" (Psalms 43:1), \"plead the widow's cause\" (Isaiah 1:17). He means that Dan will exact the vengeance of his people, all the tribes of Israel as one. The reason is that the Philistines did evil to all Israel many times — for in the days of Shamgar son of Anat they began (Judges 3:31), and in the days of Jephthah it is written (Judges 10:7), \"and He sold them into the hand of the Philistines,\" and also after Abdon son of Hillel (Judges 12:13), \"and YHWH gave them into the hand of the Philistines forty years\" (Judges 13:1) — and there was none among the judges who subdued them or defeated them at all. And even though it is written of Shamgar, \"He struck the Philistines six hundred men with an oxgoad\" (Judges 3:31), that is not vengeance, for it is not a great blow. Therefore it is written of Samson, \"and he began to save Israel from the hand of the Philistines\" (Judges 13:5). And he took Israel's vengeance from them, for he slew a multitude of them and he killed all the lords of the Philistines. And Scripture uses the word \"ידין\" (will judge) because this avenger was a judge, not a king. And it is possible that this is the opinion of Onkelos, who said, \"ביומהי יתפרק עמה\" (in his days his people will be delivered). And it is also possible that \"כאחד שבטי ישראל\" (as one of the tribes of Israel) means — like the distinguished one among the tribes, namely Judah, of whom it is said, \"your hand shall be on the neck of your enemies\" (Genesis 49:8), for this one too will prevail over his enemies and defeat them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:46:54.404787218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}